      "reason": "Reviewed false positives: shell-free argv to explicit test or governance commands; subprocess import alone is not command injection; /tmp literals are adversarial aliases or cwd/tmpfs, never insecure temporary file creation; XML parser handles only the repository SVG corpus. No scanner severity or rule globally disabled. Changed reviewed source or policy fails before scanning. 2026-11-11: reviewed fixture path migration to dated logs and .cache/ox; shell-only production contract remains unchanged. Existing suppression rules unchanged. Complete-run repair: reviewed only retained-log/cache fixture paths, a deterministic historical resource selection and missing-diagnostic assertions; executable subprocess boundaries and suppression policies unchanged. Reviewed six new native-helper/lifecycle subprocess occurrences: user-selected local binary passed as one argv element without a shell; fixed Bash test program with positional fixture paths. Fixed absolute Bash executable; only exact source hashes and native occurrences/per-file S603 accepted. 2026-11-13: maintainer requested Ec analyzer defaults. Ruff adopts Ec groups (security remains integral Bandit); old Ruff per-file exceptions removed. test_automation.py changes only the shell-layout assertion to permit unittest -m while still rejecting inline Python; subprocess boundaries and Bandit baseline unchanged. 2026-11-13 complete repair: preserve authenticated SDD validator/runner bytes; bounded Ruff I001/UP017 style dispositions and one baseline B110 validator path handler. trace_errors already reports rejected paths; no security error is accepted. Source and policy hashes enforce these reviewed inputs. Legacy CLI regression now checks manifest rejection during execution and planning without Cargo; local fixed argv to the explicit fixture wrapper, no shell=True or new trust boundary. 2026-11-15: independent review of five new B404/B603 test occurrences in instruction routes/validator: fixed sys.executable plus repository entry and disposable fixture arguments, shell=False. Baseline records only these five native occurrences and exact reviewed source hashes. Package source import/receipt bytes and validator path checks reviewed against retained preimages; no severity/rule exclusion or changed acceptance expectation. New observations pending; historical scanner hashes are not renewed. 2026-11-15 terminal progress: independent occurrence review approved exactly eight native Bandit candidates (B404 import and seven B603 calls) in the new controlled runner tests: absolute /bin/bash with fixed argv, shell=False, disposable fixture paths and internal data. Source and baseline hashes bind this disposition; all rules/severities remain enabled. Review and observed native reports: docs/validation/terminal-progress-20261115/review-security.json. This does not renew historical observations or approve the product."
    },
    "history_sha256": "4e025a01248fdfdc4023d5207e41802d1f4570fea7959fed1d0f9a967af17d83"
